\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Before \ref{ms-0001}, produce a verified inventory of what Mathlib (pinned version) provides, with exact names. Expected candidates, none assumed: \code{CategoryTheory.{Category, Functor, NatTrans, Limits, Comma, Grothendieck, MorphismProperty}}, lifting properties and the small object argument (Riou), \code{SimplexCategory}, \code{SimplicialObject}, \code{SSet} with \code{boundary}/\code{horn}, \code{SSet.KanComplex}, \code{Nerve}, truncations and skeleta, \code{Quasicategory}, joins/slices if present, any Kan–Quillen model structure material, \code{Fin} combinatorics and \code{omega}. Record for each: name, statement as we need it, gaps. The inventory is a forest node and is updated at each Mathlib bump.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Every earlier plan in this design assumed Mathlib content that had to be hedged. The inventory converts hedges into tasks.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen.}
}
